14"}, "policy_hash": "sha256:9ad00686dd2253c6ab6248bc9019c435d094832baa3fbf1faeba8adf187ec4e5", "source_label": "artin-section-contractions", "usage": "p0-locked-math-frame", "usage_source": {"after": "S", "before": "\\\\\n", "environments": ["matrix"]}}, "command": "text", "policy_entry": "p0-frame-artin-21", "slot_byte_span": {"end": 90, "start": 68}, "slot_id": "math/0001/text/0002", "source": "algebraic spaces over "}], "source": "$$\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{locally Noetherian formal} \\\\\n\\text{algebraic spaces over }S\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{An}_S,\n\\quad\\quad\nY \\longmapsto Y^{an}\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 636, "start": 456}, "source_hash": "sha256:b0f6fe59df294e9f2812777f5dc8354981e3575692d489f89584f3662daba429"}], "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "0GH7", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "} \\\\\n\\text{", "MATHSEG_0003": "}S\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{An}_S,\n\\quad\\quad\nY \\longmapsto Y^{an}\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$V$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$(Z, u', \\hat x)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{An}_S$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$Y = \\text{Spf}(k[[t]])$", "MATH_0007": "$S = \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0008": "$Y^{an}$", "MATH_0009": "$Y = \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0010": "$Y^{an}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\textit{An}_S$", "MATH_0012": "$Y$", "MATH_0013": "$Y_{red} \\to Y$", "MATH_0014": "$Y_{red}^{an} \\to Y^{an}$", "MATH_0015": "$Y^{rig} = Y^{an} \\setminus Y_{red}^{an}$", "MATH_0016": "$Y$", "MATH_0017": "$Z \\subset Y$", "MATH_0018": "$Y_{/Z} \\to Y$", "MATH_0019": "$Y_{/Z}^{an} \\to Y^{an}$", "MATH_0020": "$$\ncan : (Y_{/Z})^{rig} \\longrightarrow (Y \\setminus Z)^{an}\n$$", "MATH_0021": "$g : Y' \\to Y$", "MATH_0022": "$g^{rig} : (Y')^{rig} \\to Y^{rig}$", "MATH_0023": "$\\text{An}_S$", "MATH_0024": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n(V_{/Z})^{rig} \\ar[rr]_{can} \\ar[d]_{(g^{rig})^{-1} \\circ \\hat x^{an}} & &\n(V \\setminus Z)^{an} \\ar[d]^{(u')^{an}} \\\\\n(X'_{/T'})^{rig} \\ar[rr]^{can} & & (X' \\setminus T')^{an}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0025": "$g^{rig} : (X'_{T'})^{rig} \\to W^{rig}$", "MATH_0026": "$U' = X' \\setminus T'$", "MATH_0027": "$u'$", "MATH_0028": "$\\hat x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-contractions}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-how-to-think-compatibility}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c1cf53f82b20100332b00b73b02713c0aa3c550d532e9940046e8df38641e35c", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:c8e4f0df6772894486d376ec137c6b18a18545f18d9e0bb45ed1e4f3876d728b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:13c37e345774fa1dde659f2d17acda6eaf2490e1387a3ef9ece6362ccddbc57d", "source_text": "In Situation <REF_0001> let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian\nscheme over <MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003> be a triple satisfying (1), (2), and\n(3) above. We want to explain a way to think about the compatibility\ncondition (4). It will not be mathematically precise as we are going use\na fictitious category <MATH_0004> of analytic spaces over <MATH_0005>\nand a fictitious analytification functor\n<MATHSEG_0001>locally Noetherian formal<MATHSEG_0002>algebraic spaces over <MATHSEG_0003>\nFor example if <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>, then <MATH_0008>\nshould be thought of as an open unit disc. If <MATH_0009>, then <MATH_0010>\nis a single point. The category <MATH_0011> should have open and\nclosed immersions and we should be able to take the open complement\nof a closed. Given <MATH_0012> the morphism <MATH_0013> should induces a\nclosed immersion <MATH_0014>. We set\n<MATH_0015> equal to its open complement.\nIf <MATH_0016> is an algebraic space and if <MATH_0017> is closed, then\nthe morphism <MATH_0018> should induce an open immersion\n<MATH_0019> which in turn should induce an open immersion\n<MATH_0020>\nAlso, given a formal modification <MATH_0021> of locally Noetherian formal\nalgebraic spaces, the induced morphism <MATH_0022>\nshould be an isomorphism. Given <MATH_0023> and the analytification\nfunctor, we can consider the requirement that\n<MATH_0024>\ncommutes. This makes sense as <MATH_0025>\nis an isomorphism and <MATH_0026>. Finally, under some assumptions\nof faithfulness of the analytification functor, this requirement will\nbe equivalent to the compatibility condition formulated above.\nWe hope this will motivate the reader to think of the compatibility\nof <MATH_0027> and <MATH_0028> as the requirement that some maps be equal,\nrather than asking for the existence of a certain commutative diagram.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d048c24b2cff0a1dc8277dc8afefdde91eef89c6ab67e7279635fc4c45b384cc", "unit_id": "tag:0GID:statement"}
